<h3>MacBook Neo is So Popular That Apple Reportedly Doubled Production</h3><br/>
On an earnings call in late April, Apple's CEO Tim Cook said that customer response to the MacBook Neo was "off the charts," and the popularity of the laptop has reportedly led the company to significantly boost production.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/MacBook-Neo-on-Yellow-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1050352" /><br/>
Apple supply chain analyst Ming-Chi Kuo this week said he believes that MacBook Neo shipments to Apple were <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/03/macbook-neo-production-doubled-says-kuo/">doubled from an initial target of 5 million units to 10 million units in 2026</a> at some point after the laptop launched in March.<br/>
<br/>
The MacBook Neo is quickly reshaping the low-cost laptop segment, with companies like <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/05/29/windows-pc-industry-reacts-to-macbook-neo/">Acer, ASUS,</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/01/dell-xps-13-vs-macbook-neo/">Dell</a> reacting to the shift and in some cases already introducing their own competing products.<br/>
